      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Every runner has legitimate claims. STARDARMUS (5) has been in work for a long while and recent runs have been over more ground. Well in commission last start but couldn't finish the race off over 1400m at this track. Can bounce back over this sharper journey without surprising. PRINCE OF KHATUN (3) last appeared when third in a $125k three-year-old race at this track and trip in February. Distance specialist who is trialling in great style so a big run looks likely. GOLDEN MEADOW (7) resumes. Six-time winner at this trip and has been in the money at ten of 15 runs here. Must go in the exotics. NIGHT PEOPLE (2) has won two from five when fresh so keep him in mind first-up from a nine-month lay-off. GO JEANIE (4) also resumes. Has a fine record at Launceston and boasts two wins and two placings from five first-up runs. Strong credentials.",
